{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1096886-advice-on-time-travel","id":1096886,"title":"Advice on Time Travel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T15:35:26-07:00","id":1096886,"title":"Advice on Time Travel","content":"Hi All! <br /> <br /> I am starting a new game in the next few weeks, and I have at least 1 player starting with Time 3 and a keen interest in time travelling using Shifting Sands. <br /> <br /> Permitting Time Travel is pretty rare in RPGs, I suspect with good reason, so I cant claim to have any experience running time travel stories in the past. <br /> <br /> I was hoping the wise folks here could offer some advice on how to plan for players with these capabilities, any examples of how its come up in your games or warnings on pitfalls to avoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T17:38:00-07:00","id":1096915,"title":"","content":"It's pretty straightforward in Mage. When you go back the present freezes, you inhabit yourself from a short time ago, make some adjustments and jump back to where you were. Shifting Sands shouldn't really upset the apple cart, you can't go back terribly far unless you're willing to spend Reach. There's a potential abuse though if you use Shifting Sands inside of a long established Demesne since then you could spend as many Reach as you want to go back as many scenes as you want. To cut that off I recommend a houserule that a friend and I came up with. So, in the default version of Shifting Sands you can go back a number of turns equal to Potency, right? Keep that idea when your player decides to use Shifting Sands with the Reach option, they can go back a number of Scenes equal to Potency. This does mean they'll spend less Reach on going back further via Shifting Sands, -but- it means that they probably can't go back more than a day which should solve a lot of headaches.<br /> <br /> Other than that, control your pacing and use of the spotlight, feel free to apply the butterfly effect as long as you don't do it in a way that screws your players over and ruins their fun. You can make time travel less appealing if you have trouble with it. For instance, if you set up events in such a way that all of them are important, say the cabal just had an important meeting, but then run into combat and find themselves under-prepared the Acanthus has to decide if going back far enough to be prepared and thus sacrificing the meeting is worth it. That kind of thing isn't a &quot;Screw you!&quot; to the player, it makes their actions and decisions very meaningful. <br /> <br /> Have your NPCs that might want to cause the cabal trouble be smart, maybe they have access to Time as well and so they can anticipate the cabal's movements even when things suddenly change because the Acanthus made something different happen, or they Shield themselves from the effects of the time traveler and thus remember how things happened the first time around and change their actions accordingly. Maybe they've got Prime 2 and can Counterspell the Shifting Sands before it goes off. Maybe they've managed to develop some really bizarre arcana attainment that allows them to target the past via recordings of it rather than travelling themselves.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, Time is the win button, and that's okay. If that happens often, get used to it happening and adjust your ST style accordingly to give you and your players less headaches by using the story. <br /> <br /> Also, remember, if it hasn't happened on screen in front of your players, then it -hasn't- happened. A player's actions are the opening of Schrodinger's box, until then it's a toss up. The friend I developed that houserule with, he's been running a Mage game for over 2 years, lots of time travel has happened at one point or another. One of the biggest pains in the ass the players have had to confront is not a rolled up, statted out NPC. He's a concept that has the expertise to do what he wants and know what he needs to know to play the foil to the cabal's exploits. Things have gotten hammered out over the course of play because the player's -experienced- it, not because he had a set plan ahead of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T21:14:18-07:00","id":1096975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1096886-advice-on-time-travel?p=1096915#post1096915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a potential abuse though if you use Shifting Sands inside of a long established Demesne since then you could spend as many Reach as you want to go back as many scenes as you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things I feel bear reminding, because these are often overlooked:<br /> <br /> 1. Demesnes, like regular Verges, need to be semiotically linked to a spell to gain its Paradox-oriented benefit, since that's linked to qualifying for the Yantra bonus.<br /> <br /> 2. Shifting Sands is a non-Lasting time-travel spell and therefore subject to the same Duration concerns as Corridors of Time without the benefit of having Duration as a primary factor.<br /> <br /> Between these facts, the temporal aura, and the risks involved in skipping over the intervening time, it should generally be made clear to players that using Time magic for more involved activities than short-term troubleshooting is not done lightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T03:37:10-07:00","id":1097067,"title":"","content":"Shifting Sands is Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T07:50:40-07:00","id":1097123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1096886-advice-on-time-travel?p=1097067#post1097067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifting Sands is Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changes made while in the past are Lasting if the spell 'completes' correctly, but I believe Satchel's point is that going back in time itself is not Lasting. That is, by default with Shifting Sands you can back in time a number of turns equal to Potency (or Scenes with Reach) but the default Duration is 1 Turn, so you aren't there for all that long to make changes. It isn't like Back to the Future where traveling back is one and done unless you find a way forward again, that would be Lasting time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T11:28:58-07:00","id":1097196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1096886-advice-on-time-travel?p=1097123#post1097123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Changes made while in the past are Lasting if the spell 'completes' correctly, but I believe Satchel's point is that going back in time itself is not Lasting. That is, by default with Shifting Sands you can back in time a number of turns equal to Potency (or Scenes with Reach) but the default Duration is 1 Turn, so you aren't there for all that long to make changes. It isn't like Back to the Future where traveling back is one and done unless you find a way forward again, that would be Lasting time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aah yeah that makes sense then. If Satchel meant it like that it makes perfect sense. <br /> &quot;Real&quot; time travel to the past like in Back to the Future would be beyond the scope of awakened magic. Even with indefinite duration it would not be the same, so for that kind of time travel you need another source of magic, or perhaps archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T12:29:20-07:00","id":1097219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1096886-advice-on-time-travel?p=1097196#post1097196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aah yeah that makes sense then. If Satchel meant it like that it makes perfect sense. <br /> &quot;Real&quot; time travel to the past like in Back to the Future would be beyond the scope of awakened magic. Even with indefinite duration it would not be the same, so for that kind of time travel you need another source of magic, or perhaps archmastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Dave has said that back to the future time travel requires Archmastery or an Iris to the intended point in the past, and that Archmasters technically do it by creating their own such Irises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:43:48-07:00","id":1097302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1096886-advice-on-time-travel?p=1097219#post1097219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure Dave has said that back to the future time travel requires Archmastery or an Iris to the intended point in the past</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Subjects cannot be sent back to<br /> periods outside their own lifetime. Such unfettered time travel<br /> is the stuff of legend, temporal Irises, and whispers about the<br /> powers of archmages. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:58:55-07:00","id":1097341,"title":"","content":"On the actual advice front:<br /> <br /> Be prepared to either re-run scenes or hand-wave changes based on logical extrapolation. I'm not sure how your other players will feel about replaying scenes when the Time mage goes back in time; my group wanted to play it by ear and replay some scenes and hand-wave others depending on what happened and how important it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T18:11:18-07:00","id":1097378,"title":"","content":"Here's my attempt at advice;<br /> \u200b1-Mage is about mysteries and while time travel can be a powerful tool for decrypting the past it doesn't have to be an absolute deal breaker. Even some of the steps an actor may take to hide information from non time travelers will help, it doesn't do much good to go back and witness a murder first hand if the killer is wearing a mask and you can't see under it.<br /> \u200b2-A time traveler inhabits his own body in the past, this means that even while traveling through time he can only be in one place at a time. That means he can only change one past event at any given time, if he travels back again to change something else at that time he undoes his earlier action. So give him several options and make him choose which one he wants to change the most, the rest he will have to live with, unless of course he comes up with a brilliant plan that upends everything for which he should be rewarded.<br /> \u200b3-Dr. Beckett's 'string theory'; you can only travel back to points within your own life span. This means that anything that happened before you were born is off limits. Sure you could go back in time and deal with the fallout, perhaps succeeding in preventing some of it, but you still have to work within the limits provided. Time is not a magic button that allows you to rewrite history to go the way you want.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs far as forcing the other players to redo everything, if the change your time traveler makes shouldn't really impact what they did then don't make them start over. If the other characters succeeded or failed at something that wouldn't be effected don't force the 'Butterfly effect', just keep the original results.<br /> If you lock the front door of a house that shouldn't stop people from fleeing out the back if that's what they did the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 05-26-2017, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}